WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.025
Tutorial one.

00:00:01.025 --> 00:00:02.207
Player scoring.

00:00:02.207 --> 00:00:05.674
Open Competition, then Fixtures and results.

00:00:05.674 --> 00:00:09.299
Choose the correct tournament stage and round.

00:00:09.299 --> 00:00:14.186
Search by player name, code or team, and select Show fixtures.

00:00:14.186 --> 00:00:17.653
Check both opponents and the best-of length.

00:00:17.653 --> 00:00:21.830
On the correct match, select Enter or correct result.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.174
Keep Match result set to Played.

00:00:24.174 --> 00:00:29.814
Select the winner of Game one, then each following game in the order actually

00:00:29.814 --> 00:00:30.327
played.

00:00:30.327 --> 00:00:32.964
The next game appears automatically.

00:00:32.964 --> 00:00:37.798
A best of three needs two wins, best of five needs three, and best

00:00:37.798 --> 00:00:39.263
of seven needs four.

00:00:39.263 --> 00:00:42.632
Stop as soon as one player reaches the target.

00:00:42.632 --> 00:00:44.610
Leave unplayed games blank.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.273
Either player can win.

00:00:46.273 --> 00:00:50.960
In best of three, the completed scores are two nil or two one.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.815
In best of five, three nil, three one or three two.

00:00:54.815 --> 00:00:59.426
In best of seven, four nil, four one, four two or four three.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:03.584
Any game order works if you stop at the winning target.

00:01:03.584 --> 00:01:09.480
Try other odd lengths, from one to ninety nine, in the manual's practice area.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.970
Check the series result and winner.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:15.741
You can attach a P N G, J PEG or Web P screenshot, up

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:17.021
to four megabytes.

00:01:17.021 --> 00:01:22.571
Select Save and confirm when checked, or Save for review for a later decision.

00:01:22.571 --> 00:01:27.266
An unfinished normal series cannot be saved as a completed result.

00:01:27.266 --> 00:01:30.254
Only finalized results count in standings.

00:01:30.254 --> 00:01:34.950
A league win earns three points, a draw one each, and a loss zero.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:40.399
For a draw, the stage must have Draws allowed after review saved in its

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:40.859
rules.

00:01:40.859 --> 00:01:41.780
Choose Draw.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:48.534
Keep Record games played checked only if games were completed, and select those winners.

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:52.141
Neither player may already have won the series.

00:01:52.141 --> 00:01:57.437
Add a note and save for review, or confirm after checking the policy.

00:01:57.437 --> 00:02:00.660
A drawn knockout has no winner to advance.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:06.050
For a no-show or forfeit, first check that forfeits are allowed with a reason.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:08.262
Select the player who forfeited.

00:02:08.262 --> 00:02:10.749
If player A forfeits, player B wins.

00:02:10.749 --> 00:02:14.965
Record any completed games, or leave games off for a no-show.

00:02:14.965 --> 00:02:18.558
Enter a clear reason and check the displayed winner.

00:02:18.558 --> 00:02:25.400
For disconnections or both players absent, apply the organiser's policy before choosing an outcome.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:31.171
To correct a score, reopen Enter or correct result and change the affected game's

00:02:31.171 --> 00:02:31.669
winner.

00:02:31.669 --> 00:02:36.941
Clear this game and later games removes that game and everything after it.

00:02:36.941 --> 00:02:39.649
Explain changes to an accepted result.

00:02:39.649 --> 00:02:45.776
Use Result history and review to inspect versions and evidence, then accept, reject or

00:02:45.776 --> 00:02:47.699
dispute a submitted result.

00:02:47.699 --> 00:02:50.406
Rejecting or disputing needs a reason.

00:02:50.406 --> 00:02:52.900
Earlier versions remain in history.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:58.208
For knockout matches, keep Advance the confirmed winner checked when confirming.

00:02:58.208 --> 00:03:02.123
You can also advance later from Match schedule and actions.

00:03:02.123 --> 00:03:06.967
Byes use Advance player without an opponent, with no invented game score.

00:03:06.967 --> 00:03:12.939
If an earlier correction changes downstream opponents, ask an admin to resolve the bracket

00:03:12.939 --> 00:03:16.323
changes before scoring or advancing the next match.

00:03:16.323 --> 00:03:20.202
Use the written manual for dispute resolution and troubleshooting.
